{"step_index":144,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:35:04Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:35:04+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:35:04+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Metric.lean`\nTotal Lines: 455\nTotal Bytes: 17223\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: /-\n2: Copyright (c) 2022 Kyle Miller. All rights reserved.\n3: Released under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.\n4: Authors: Kyle Miller, Vincent Beffara, Rida Hamadani, Nelson Spence\n5: -/\n6: module\n7: \n8: public import Mathlib.Combinatorics.SimpleGraph.Connectivity.Connected\n9: public import Mathlib.Data.ENat.Lattice\n10: \n11: /-!\n12: # Graph metric\n13: \n14: This module defines the `SimpleGraph.edist` function, which takes pairs of vertices to the length of\n15: the shortest walk between them, or `⊤` if they are disconnected. It also defines `SimpleGraph.dist`\n16: which is the `ℕ`-valued version of `SimpleGraph.edist`, and `SimpleGraph.ball` which is the open\n17: ball in the graph extended metric.\n18: \n19: ## Main definitions\n20: \n21: - `SimpleGraph.edist` is the graph extended metric.\n22: - `SimpleGraph.dist` is the graph metric.\n23: - `SimpleGraph.ball` is the open ball of a given radius around a vertex.\n24: \n25: ## TODO\n26: \n27: - Provide an additional computable version of `SimpleGraph.dist`\n28:   for when `G` is connected.\n29: \n30: - When directed graphs exist, a directed notion of distance,\n31:   likely `ENat`-valued.\n32: \n33: ## Tags\n34: \n35: graph metric, distance, ball\n36: \n37: -/\n38: \n39: @[expose] public section\n40: \n41: assert_not_exists Field\n42: \n43: name